1249
00:53:21,784 --> 00:53:23,683
-No, I'm going to kill you.

1250
00:53:23,717 --> 00:53:26,962
-You unscrupulous pig!

1251
00:53:26,996 --> 00:53:29,482
-Mummy's home.
Now you're gonna get it.

1252
00:53:32,485 --> 00:53:34,935
-Bullets bounce right off.

1253
00:53:34,970 --> 00:53:38,111
-Or go right through.

1254
00:53:38,145 --> 00:53:39,664
-Doesn't really matter.

1255
00:53:39,699 --> 00:53:42,357
Yeah, keep shooting, Bruno.
It's gonna work, really.

1256
00:53:42,391 --> 00:53:45,325
-Aah!

1257
00:53:45,360 --> 00:53:48,294
Ah!

1258
00:53:48,328 --> 00:53:50,123
-Beautiful. 
-[Screams]

1259
00:53:50,157 --> 00:53:52,263
-Oops.

1260
00:53:52,298 --> 00:53:53,989
-Right where it hurts.

1261
00:53:54,023 --> 00:53:56,923
-On the floor.

1262
00:53:56,957 --> 00:53:58,718
-Aah!

1263
00:53:58,752 --> 00:54:01,030
-He's wearing a smoking jacket,
you guys.

1264
00:54:01,065 --> 00:54:04,517
[Gunshots]

1265
00:54:04,551 --> 00:54:06,691
-I'm out.
-Whoa!

1266
00:54:06,726 --> 00:54:08,279
-There's some furniture
he missed.

1267
00:54:08,314 --> 00:54:10,971
-Aah!

1268
00:54:11,006 --> 00:54:12,835
-Ooh.

1269
00:54:12,870 --> 00:54:14,699
-I saved the Beaver.

1270
00:54:16,770 --> 00:54:18,600
I saved Flora.

1271
00:54:18,634 --> 00:54:24,019
♪♪

1272
00:54:24,053 --> 00:54:29,196
♪♪

1273
00:54:29,231 --> 00:54:30,543
-Look out.
-Come on, Beav,

1274
00:54:30,577 --> 00:54:32,027
let's go check this out.

1275
00:54:32,061 --> 00:54:37,722
♪♪

1276
00:54:37,757 --> 00:54:40,277
-They seem stunned. 
-No!

1277
00:54:40,311 --> 00:54:41,830
Doctor, help me!

1278
00:54:41,864 --> 00:54:43,280
Can't you hear?!

1279
00:54:43,314 --> 00:54:45,903
No! 
Help me!

1280
00:54:45,937 --> 00:54:48,319
-Yeah, you're first on our list
of people to help.

1281
00:54:48,354 --> 00:54:51,322
-Please help me! 
Help me!

1282
00:54:51,357 --> 00:54:53,013
-Then we realized 
who the criminals were

1283
00:54:53,048 --> 00:54:54,498
and settled accounts with them.

1284
00:54:54,532 --> 00:54:56,189
Then when he saw the doctor 
trying to escape,

1285
00:54:56,223 --> 00:54:57,397
he picked him up 
like a rag doll

1286
00:54:57,432 --> 00:54:59,054
and threw him into 
a pit full of rattlers

1287
00:54:59,088 --> 00:55:01,574
-Every good laboratory
has a pit full of rattlers.

1288
00:55:01,608 --> 00:55:03,127
-[Screaming]

1289
00:55:03,161 --> 00:55:06,406
-Or would that be a bad touch?
-Yeah, I think so.

1290
00:55:06,441 --> 00:55:10,997
-We were tired, but it was
a good kind of tired.

1291
00:55:11,031 --> 00:55:12,654
-Mummy's done cleaning.

1292
00:55:12,688 --> 00:55:14,103
-Afterwards with 
the breastplate

1293
00:55:14,138 --> 00:55:15,760
and the bracelet in his hand,

1294
00:55:15,795 --> 00:55:18,798
he slowly shuffled away 
into the darkness

1295
00:55:18,832 --> 00:55:21,318
and soon was lost from sight.

1296
00:55:21,352 --> 00:55:22,871
I'll never forget 
the strong affection

1297
00:55:22,905 --> 00:55:24,459
I had for Flora's father.

1298
00:55:24,493 --> 00:55:26,461
Such a kind man 
who's intelligent advice

1299
00:55:26,495 --> 00:55:28,014
brought about our salvation.

1300
00:55:28,048 --> 00:55:30,603
-And the mummy? 
Went back to the pyramid?

1301
00:55:30,637 --> 00:55:32,605
-No, he had two nights
at the Copa.

1302
00:55:32,639 --> 00:55:33,778
-The explosion destroyed 
his temple.

1303
00:55:33,813 --> 00:55:35,987
He had no reason to go there.

1304
00:55:36,022 --> 00:55:38,369
-In that case, can't you tell 
us where he is?

1305
00:55:38,404 --> 00:55:40,889
-Permit me to continue.
-Hey, it's your movie.

1306
00:55:40,923 --> 00:55:42,822
-All these tragic happenings 
couldn't go unattended.

1307
00:55:42,856 --> 00:55:46,998
So I went to the police and they heard the whole story.

1308
00:55:47,033 --> 00:55:48,828
Then I returned to Krupp's 
hideout accompanied

1309
00:55:48,862 --> 00:55:51,348
by the chief of police 
and a couple of his men.

1310
00:55:51,382 --> 00:55:53,280
You can imagine our surprise 
when we discovered

1311
00:55:53,315 --> 00:55:56,594
the place was completely empty.-Except for all this garbage.

1312
00:55:56,629 --> 00:56:02,497
♪♪

1313
00:56:02,531 --> 00:56:04,947
-The laboratory had been 
dismantled

1314
00:56:04,982 --> 00:56:07,225
and the bodies of the criminals that at the mummy had killed

1315
00:56:07,260 --> 00:56:10,781
had also disappeared.
-They were dismantled as well.

1316
00:56:13,818 --> 00:56:16,752
Continuing our search, 
we hurried to the snake pit.

1317
00:56:16,787 --> 00:56:19,721
I was awestruck when I realized that the body of Dr. Krupp

1318
00:56:19,755 --> 00:56:21,032
was no longer down there.

1319
00:56:21,067 --> 00:56:22,240
-Aww.

1320
00:56:22,275 --> 00:56:23,310
-Then to our horror, 
we discovered

1321
00:56:23,345 --> 00:56:24,415
that there was a small door

1322
00:56:24,450 --> 00:56:26,141
in the back wall of the pit

1323
00:56:26,175 --> 00:56:28,488
through which the doctor could 
have escaped.

1324
00:56:28,523 --> 00:56:30,179
-He was such a large man.
How could he?

1325
00:56:30,214 --> 00:56:32,216
-Obviously, the doctor 
had escaped,

1326
00:56:32,250 --> 00:56:34,391
and strangely I don't think he'd been bitten.

1327
00:56:34,425 --> 00:56:36,462
-The man's running loose. 
-So that would mean

1328
00:56:36,496 --> 00:56:39,223
that the doctor kept trying 
to combine those articles

1329
00:56:39,257 --> 00:56:40,983
so that he could locate 
the treasure.

1330
00:56:41,018 --> 00:56:42,813
-You're right, my friend, 
he did just that.

1331
00:56:42,847 --> 00:56:45,436
He began to bother us 
a couple of weeks later.

1332
00:56:45,471 --> 00:56:47,680
It happened quite suddenly, 
you see.

1333
00:56:47,714 --> 00:56:50,303
One dark night.

1334
00:56:50,337 --> 00:56:52,029
-This is the house.

1335
00:56:54,997 --> 00:56:56,585
-Do you really think this 
plan of yours

1336
00:56:56,620 --> 00:56:58,725
is gonna work, Doc?

1337
00:56:58,760 --> 00:57:01,935
-You'll see. 
Now, I want you to be quiet.

1338
00:57:01,970 --> 00:57:04,317
Keep still and don't make 
the slightest noise.

1339
00:57:04,351 --> 00:57:06,423
-Peas and carrots, peas and
carrots, peas and carrots.

1340
00:57:06,457 --> 00:57:07,872
[All grumbling]

1341
00:57:07,907 --> 00:57:11,289
-I wish that you 
come to my side.

1342
00:57:14,016 --> 00:57:16,467
Flora, I command you 
to come to me.

1343
00:57:16,502 --> 00:57:18,711
-I think he's using teleflora.

1344
00:57:18,745 --> 00:57:24,648
-Flora, I command you 
to come to me.

1345
00:57:24,682 --> 00:57:29,480
-Use the door bell.
-Doorknob.

1346
00:57:29,515 --> 00:57:33,484
-Flora, are you listening? 
Come here to me.

1347
00:57:33,519 --> 00:57:36,142
-Is he speaking into his glove?

1348
00:57:36,176 --> 00:57:37,799
-Must be a party line.

1349
00:57:37,833 --> 00:57:42,217
♪♪

1350
00:57:42,251 --> 00:57:45,392
-976 Flora?

1351
00:57:45,427 --> 00:57:50,639
♪♪

1352
00:57:50,674 --> 00:57:53,193
-Stand up.
-Wear something sheer.

1353
00:57:53,228 --> 00:57:56,611
-Put on a housecoat. -Flora, do not try to fight it.

1354
00:57:56,645 --> 00:57:58,578
Come here.

1355
00:58:01,132 --> 00:58:05,378
-Notice you never
actually see her get dressed.

1356
00:58:05,412 --> 00:58:07,794
Open the door this time,
don't walk through it.

1357
00:58:09,831 --> 00:58:12,040
-Good girl.
-Well done.

1358
00:58:12,074 --> 00:58:14,491
-That'll save some repair work.

1359
00:58:14,525 --> 00:58:17,252
-Hey, close it all the way.
Were you born in a barn?

1360
00:58:17,286 --> 00:58:20,393
-Flora, do not try to fight it. Come here.

1361
00:58:23,223 --> 00:58:25,640
-Step, step, step.

1362
00:58:25,674 --> 00:58:28,263
Kick, step, kick.

1363
00:58:30,886 --> 00:58:35,684
-Right, left, right, left.

1364
00:58:35,719 --> 00:58:39,412
Okay, it's all flat
from here, Flora.

1365
00:58:39,446 --> 00:58:40,758
Oh.

1366
00:58:40,793 --> 00:58:44,935
She's not falling for it.
-No.

1367
00:58:44,969 --> 00:58:49,077
-She's no pushover.

1368
00:58:49,111 --> 00:58:52,011
Loud clock.

1369
00:58:52,045 --> 00:58:53,909
And kettle drum.

1370
00:58:55,946 --> 00:58:58,086
-Flora, are you listening?

1371
00:58:58,120 --> 00:59:03,505
I command you to come to me.
-I'm comin', I'm comin'.

1372
00:59:06,646 --> 00:59:10,581
-Flora, you ought to do 
as I command. Come here.

1373
00:59:10,616 --> 00:59:12,479
-Digging for gold,
Bruno?

1374
00:59:12,514 --> 00:59:18,416
♪♪

1375
00:59:18,451 --> 00:59:20,557
-Okay, Bruno, when she passes
in front of the car,

1376
00:59:20,591 --> 00:59:23,629
honk really loud.
-[Imitates car horn]

1377
00:59:26,735 --> 00:59:29,289
-Love me
and my deformed friend.

1378
00:59:29,324 --> 00:59:30,808
-You can hear the waves 
that are being

1379
00:59:30,843 --> 00:59:32,465
sent out by that mummy, 
can you not?

1380
00:59:32,499 --> 00:59:34,087
-And the guy in the car. 
-I know well that you are able

1381
00:59:34,122 --> 00:59:36,607
to lead us to him. 
-Yes, I can.

1382
00:59:36,642 --> 00:59:39,092
-Then tell us, 
where is Popoca?

1383
00:59:39,127 --> 00:59:40,922
-The "Beer Barrel Popoca?"

1384
00:59:40,956 --> 00:59:44,304
-In the ancient cemetery. 
-Come with me.

1385
00:59:44,339 --> 00:59:49,689
♪♪

1386
00:59:49,724 --> 00:59:51,898
-Is the ancient cemetery
denominational?

1387
00:59:51,933 --> 00:59:57,076
♪♪

1388
00:59:57,110 --> 00:59:58,733
-Meanwhile, in the
ancient cemetery,

1389
00:59:58,767 --> 01:00:00,010
they were looking for the mummy.

1390
01:00:00,044 --> 01:00:03,013
But first, let's kick over
some gravestones.

1391
01:00:03,047 --> 01:00:04,497
-You know, that would
make another

1392
01:00:04,531 --> 01:00:07,189
excellent miniature
golf course.

1393
01:00:07,224 --> 01:00:09,536
Like the other movie.

1394
01:00:09,571 --> 01:00:12,022
-Each hole would be deadly.

1395
01:00:12,056 --> 01:00:13,368
-[Chuckles]

1396
01:00:13,402 --> 01:00:15,266
That last step is a doozy.

1397
01:00:15,301 --> 01:00:17,337
-Low overhead.

1398
01:00:17,372 --> 01:00:19,443
-But grave consequences.

1399
01:00:19,477 --> 01:00:21,997
-Yikes.
-Sorry.

1400
01:00:22,032 --> 01:00:24,379
-I'll shut you off.
-Don't do it.

1401
01:00:24,413 --> 01:00:25,967
-Come on, Bruno. Keep up.

1402
01:00:26,001 --> 01:00:28,348
And stop picking your nose.

1403
01:00:28,383 --> 01:00:29,556
Look, Peter Graves.

1404
01:00:29,591 --> 01:00:32,180
[Laughs]

1405
01:00:32,214 --> 01:00:34,285
-Who's buried in Peter's grave.

1406
01:00:34,320 --> 01:00:36,011
-James Arness.

1407
01:00:36,046 --> 01:00:41,638
♪♪

1408
01:00:41,672 --> 01:00:42,846
-What are you doing here?

1409
01:00:42,880 --> 01:00:45,745
Answer me. 
What are you doing here?

1410
01:00:45,780 --> 01:00:49,784
-We're hitting people. 
Come now, Flora.

1411
01:00:49,818 --> 01:00:52,303
-Must have been a disposable
character, I think.

1412
01:00:52,338 --> 01:00:57,723
♪♪

1413
01:00:57,757 --> 01:01:00,484
-Shuffle, shuffle.

1414
01:01:00,518 --> 01:01:01,968
Step, step, step.

1415
01:01:02,003 --> 01:01:03,832
-No need to hurry.

1416
01:01:03,867 --> 01:01:06,732
The plot will support all
of this sort of slowness.

1417
01:01:06,766 --> 01:01:11,081
-Lions and tigers and bears,
oh my.

1418
01:01:11,115 --> 01:01:14,601
Lions and tigers
and bears, oh my.

1419
01:01:14,636 --> 01:01:17,087
Lions and tigers and bears,
oh my.

1420
01:01:17,121 --> 01:01:18,813
-Lions and t--

1421
01:01:18,847 --> 01:01:24,335
♪♪

1422
01:01:24,370 --> 01:01:29,858
♪♪

1423
01:01:29,893 --> 01:01:31,688
-You see, this
will be our new home.

1424
01:01:31,722 --> 01:01:33,206
You'll see,
there'll be you and me,

1425
01:01:33,241 --> 01:01:34,552
and Bruno makes three.

1426
01:01:34,587 --> 01:01:36,865
-And my little deformed friend.

1427
01:01:38,729 --> 01:01:43,389
♪♪

1428
01:01:43,423 --> 01:01:46,323
-Is this the place? 
-Yes.

1429
01:01:49,188 --> 01:01:51,086
-Knock twice.
Tell 'em Sam sent ya.

1430
01:01:53,571 --> 01:01:56,436
-Shh! You trying to
wake the dead?

1431
01:01:59,508 --> 01:02:00,924
-It's open.

1432
01:02:05,583 --> 01:02:08,345
At least carry her
across the threshold.

1433
01:02:08,379 --> 01:02:11,866
-Sure am glad Flora wore
her phosphorescent dress.

1434
01:02:11,900 --> 01:02:13,591
-Don't you know that's the curseof the money, Cr--

1435
01:02:13,626 --> 01:02:15,732
mummy, Crow?
-Curse of the mummy?

1436
01:02:15,766 --> 01:02:18,251
-Yeah, it's being --
not being able to dress

1437
01:02:18,286 --> 01:02:21,220
when you rob a grave.
-I hate that.

1438
01:02:21,254 --> 01:02:23,774
I've had this dream before,
I'm in my pajamas,

1439
01:02:23,809 --> 01:02:30,022
I'm in a crypt, I'm being chasedby a big banana.

1440
01:02:30,056 --> 01:02:32,921
-Oh, man, his face looks
like cottage cheese.

1441
01:02:32,956 --> 01:02:35,096
It looks like a diet plate.

1442
01:02:35,130 --> 01:02:39,686
-You devil. You stinking devil.

1443
01:02:39,721 --> 01:02:46,728
Oh, I'd like to chop your 
rotten flesh to pieces.

1444
01:02:46,763 --> 01:02:49,696
-Bruno, stop letting hate
run your life.

1445
01:02:49,731 --> 01:02:51,491
-Who's he's hiding
his face from?

1446
01:02:51,526 --> 01:02:53,148
-Uh, his agent, I think.

1447
01:02:53,183 --> 01:02:55,737
-I'm going to make 
my experiment.

1448
01:02:55,772 --> 01:02:57,359
So we must wait.

1449
01:02:57,394 --> 01:03:00,017
-Wait? Wait!

1450
01:03:00,052 --> 01:03:03,434
When I got so much hate eaten 
down deep inside of my guts,

1451
01:03:03,469 --> 01:03:05,505
you ain't got no idea 
what it is to live like this.

1452
01:03:05,540 --> 01:03:08,785
-Oh, man, look, they taped
plastic puke to his face.

1453
01:03:08,819 --> 01:03:13,168
-Just because of that 
stinking monster.

1454
01:03:13,203 --> 01:03:16,033
-Your face could hold a
three-day rain, Bruno.

1455
01:03:16,068 --> 01:03:18,449
-I promise you 
that he'll be destroyed.

1456
01:03:18,484 --> 01:03:20,831
-[Whimpers and sobs]

1457
01:03:20,866 --> 01:03:26,043
-But give me time. 
Just a little time.

1458
01:03:26,078 --> 01:03:29,184
It won't be too long before 
you can have your revenge.

1459
01:03:29,219 --> 01:03:31,014
Let me get 
the breastplate first.

1460
01:03:31,048 --> 01:03:33,292
And the bracelet.

1461
01:03:33,326 --> 01:03:35,259
-It looks like it scabbed
over nicely.

1462
01:03:35,294 --> 01:03:40,023
-And yet so far because 
I can't touch them.

1463
01:03:40,057 --> 01:03:42,439
It's too dangerous to do it.

1464
01:03:42,473 --> 01:03:47,858
He'll wake up in an instant 
and destroy us.

1465
01:03:47,893 --> 01:03:49,618
-Sounds okay to me.

1466
01:03:49,653 --> 01:03:51,793
-But I get them back.

1467
01:03:51,828 --> 01:03:53,588
I swear it.

1468
01:03:53,622 --> 01:03:59,594
No matter how long it takes me, you devilish mummy.

1469
01:03:59,628 --> 01:04:01,389
-He looks like Mr. French.

1470
01:04:01,423 --> 01:04:02,977
-Line?

1471
01:04:03,011 --> 01:04:05,876
♪♪

1472
01:04:05,911 --> 01:04:09,466
-Come on, we'd better go now.

1473
01:04:09,500 --> 01:04:11,709
We'll be needing 
a lot of time

1474
01:04:11,744 --> 01:04:16,680
if the plan I have 
is going to work out.

1475
01:04:16,714 --> 01:04:17,888
-Anything you say.

1476
01:04:17,923 --> 01:04:21,685
-Can and will be used
against you.

1477
01:04:21,719 --> 01:04:23,549
-Come, Flora.

1478
01:04:23,583 --> 01:04:30,211
♪♪

1479
01:04:30,245 --> 01:04:33,214
-Wow. Lot of good
acting in that scene.

1480
01:04:33,248 --> 01:04:35,802
Joel, what was the point of
this little, uh,

1481
01:04:35,837 --> 01:04:38,460
little scene here?
-I don't know.

1482
01:04:38,495 --> 01:04:40,566
I think they're just staking
out a location to come

1483
01:04:40,600 --> 01:04:43,362
and shoot here later when theyhave something meaningful to do.

1484
01:04:43,396 --> 01:04:46,330
-Oh.-You know, I really dig ya, hon.

1485
01:04:46,365 --> 01:04:49,023
Can I call you again?

1486
01:04:49,057 --> 01:04:50,783
-You think he'll kiss her now

1487
01:04:50,817 --> 01:04:52,923
or wait till he gets
to the door?

1488
01:04:52,958 --> 01:04:54,925
-Always a better policy
to kiss on the steps.

1489
01:04:54,960 --> 01:04:57,134
-Ah.
-Or by the car.

1490
01:04:57,169 --> 01:04:59,240
-Or under the car.
-Or on the mouth.

1491
01:04:59,274 --> 01:05:01,863
-Ew. 
-Go up to your room

1492
01:05:01,898 --> 01:05:03,520
and you'll go to sleep,

1493
01:05:03,554 --> 01:05:06,972
and when you awaken, you'll act quite normally.

1494
01:05:07,006 --> 01:05:10,216
-You'll be refreshed
and invigorated.

1495
01:05:10,251 --> 01:05:11,769
-Do you understand?

1496
01:05:11,804 --> 01:05:15,083
You won't recall a thing.

1497
01:05:15,118 --> 01:05:17,361
Now walk.

1498
01:05:17,396 --> 01:05:19,260
-Like an Egyptian. 
-Go on.

1499
01:05:19,294 --> 01:05:21,227
-Bruno, do that thing
with the car horn again.

1500
01:05:21,262 --> 01:05:22,780
I love that bit.

1501
01:05:22,815 --> 01:05:24,644
-[Imitates car horn]

1502
01:05:24,679 --> 01:05:26,750
-[Chuckles]
She falls for it every time.

1503
01:05:26,784 --> 01:05:36,725
♪♪

1504
01:05:36,760 --> 01:05:44,941
♪♪

1505
01:05:46,494 --> 01:05:51,948
-Done this scene before,
only at night.

1506
01:05:51,982 --> 01:05:54,916
-♪ I feel pretty 
-Well, good morning.

1507
01:05:54,951 --> 01:05:56,297
-♪ Oh, so pretty 
-Good morning, sweetheart.

1508
01:05:56,331 --> 01:05:57,884
You must have been very tired.

1509
01:05:57,919 --> 01:06:00,025
We were waiting down here
to have breakfast with you.

1510
01:06:00,059 --> 01:06:02,959
We could both eat a horse
-Bacon and eggs like always?

1511
01:06:02,993 --> 01:06:07,515
-Nothing for me, Maria. I have
a terrible headache, dear.

1512
01:06:07,549 --> 01:06:10,069
-What's that you've got
on your gown?

1513
01:06:10,104 --> 01:06:11,450
-It's all dirty.

1514
01:06:11,484 --> 01:06:13,072
-Looks like dead, dried flesh.

1515
01:06:13,107 --> 01:06:15,316
-You've been down in the cellar.

1516
01:06:15,350 --> 01:06:18,112
-No, sweetheart. I don't know.

1517
01:06:18,146 --> 01:06:20,562
-But look at your slippers.
They're all muddy.

1518
01:06:20,597 --> 01:06:21,667
-And you pitted out your gown.

1519
01:06:21,701 --> 01:06:23,186
-Hold on.
What have you been up to?

1520
01:06:23,220 --> 01:06:24,704
-Just cavorting with mummies
all night.

1521
01:06:24,739 --> 01:06:25,947
-It's funny.
These are new slippers.

1522
01:06:25,982 --> 01:06:27,155
I just bought them,

1523
01:06:27,190 --> 01:06:29,019
and now they're dirty.
-And so are you!

1524
01:06:29,054 --> 01:06:30,641
-I think you went out
last night.

1525
01:06:30,676 --> 01:06:32,885
-No. After I took my bath,

1526
01:06:32,919 --> 01:06:34,783
I went to bed
because I was tired.

1527
01:06:34,818 --> 01:06:37,269
-Yes, but you got up later on,
didn't you?

1528
01:06:37,303 --> 01:06:38,960
-I did?
-Who's the kid?

1529
01:06:38,995 --> 01:06:40,444
-No.
-Yes.

1530
01:06:40,479 --> 01:06:44,586
Because I woke up a couple of
times and you were not in bed.

1531
01:06:44,621 --> 01:06:47,003
-No, you're mistaken, darling.
I assure you.

1532
01:06:47,037 --> 01:06:48,728
-Get that kid out of there.

1533
01:06:48,763 --> 01:06:50,799
-You went out last night.
Honest, Mom.

1534
01:06:50,834 --> 01:06:53,319
-Come on. Let's forget the wholething for now, all right?

1535
01:06:53,354 --> 01:06:55,011
-Floyd looks confused.
-Remember,

1536
01:06:55,045 --> 01:06:57,289
she has a great imagination.

1537
01:06:57,323 --> 01:06:59,325
Tell me,
has your headache passed?

1538
01:06:59,360 --> 01:07:02,156
-No. I'm going to lie down
for a while.

1539
01:07:02,190 --> 01:07:03,467
Excuse me, please.

1540
01:07:03,502 --> 01:07:05,400
-And I don't like the smell
of this conversation.

1541
01:07:05,435 --> 01:07:07,230
-You children go on
and have your breakfast.

1542
01:07:07,264 --> 01:07:09,059
-Yes, Daddy.

1543
01:07:09,094 --> 01:07:12,821
-Come on, Pinacate.
I want to talk to you.

1544
01:07:12,856 --> 01:07:15,721
-Oh, boy.
What a liar you are!

1545
01:07:15,755 --> 01:07:17,757
-You shut your big mouth!
You're the liar!

1546
01:07:17,792 --> 01:07:19,863
-You can't even act yourself
out of a paper bag.

1547
01:07:19,897 --> 01:07:22,762
You'll never work
in Coral Gables again.

1548
01:07:22,797 --> 01:07:25,041
-I'm very worried.

1549
01:07:25,075 --> 01:07:26,352
This attitude
that we've observed

1550
01:07:26,387 --> 01:07:28,389
in Flora is not normal.

1551
01:07:28,423 --> 01:07:29,804
What's more, I'm afraid that
The Bat"

1552
01:07:29,838 --> 01:07:31,081
has something to do with this.

1553
01:07:31,116 --> 01:07:32,531
-Maybe she should choke up
on it a little bit.

1554
01:07:32,565 --> 01:07:34,774
-You really think that child
was telling the truth about it

1555
01:07:34,809 --> 01:07:37,156
and that her mother got up
and went out?

1556
01:07:37,191 --> 01:07:39,848
-Yes, it's quite probable.

1557
01:07:39,883 --> 01:07:43,507
But Flora insisted she didn't
leave her bed for a second.

1558
01:07:43,542 --> 01:07:45,544
-Because she can't recall
anything.

1559
01:07:45,578 --> 01:07:49,237
When she got up last night,
she was sleeping.

1560
01:07:49,272 --> 01:07:52,999
-I don't understand it.
It seems impossible.

1561
01:07:53,034 --> 01:07:55,899
-I'll tell you what I think --
she was hypnotized

1562
01:07:55,933 --> 01:07:58,729
and could be under
post-hypnotic suggestion.

1563
01:07:58,764 --> 01:08:00,593
So it seems to me
that The Bat controls her

1564
01:08:00,628 --> 01:08:03,009
from a distance.
-With sonar.

1565
01:08:03,044 --> 01:08:05,081
-It's logical.
-What a sleuth.

1566
01:08:05,115 --> 01:08:07,635
-This strange attitude in Flora

1567
01:08:07,669 --> 01:08:10,120
indicated that unscrupulous
villain Krupp

1568
01:08:10,155 --> 01:08:12,122
made her leave the house
during the night.

1569
01:08:12,157 --> 01:08:13,675
-But where did they go to?

1570
01:08:13,710 --> 01:08:15,470
-Can't you guess
what he's trying to do?

1571
01:08:15,505 --> 01:08:16,575
-No.

1572
01:08:16,609 --> 01:08:18,059
-You certainly know
what he's after --

1573
01:08:18,094 --> 01:08:19,302
The breastplate.

1574
01:08:19,336 --> 01:08:20,958
-And besides that, the bracelet.

1575
01:08:20,993 --> 01:08:23,064
-And the snappy Coco Chanel
pantsuit.

1576
01:08:23,099 --> 01:08:25,308
-And you think that she
was made to go along with Krupp

1577
01:08:25,342 --> 01:08:27,931
and he wanted her
to guide him to find the mummy?

1578
01:08:27,965 --> 01:08:30,140
-Exactly.
And you and I must go there.

1579
01:08:30,175 --> 01:08:33,074
I'm going to find out if that
scoundrel stole those objects.

1580
01:08:33,109 --> 01:08:34,524
-But that will be difficult.

1581
01:08:34,558 --> 01:08:36,974
You can't investigate
without any clues.

1582
01:08:37,009 --> 01:08:38,079
-Floyd's a great barber,

1583
01:08:38,114 --> 01:08:40,564
but not a very good detective.
-Yes.

1584
01:08:40,599 --> 01:08:42,635
-Neither of them
are very good actors.

1585
01:08:42,670 --> 01:08:44,154
-Well, that goes without saying.

1586
01:08:44,189 --> 01:08:48,469
-He smokes very well, though.

1587
01:08:48,503 --> 01:08:51,161
-If loving you is wrong,
I don't want to be right.

1588
01:08:51,196 --> 01:08:53,405
-Suppose we took her slippers
to the laboratory

1589
01:08:53,439 --> 01:08:55,821
to have that mud analyzed?

1590
01:08:55,855 --> 01:08:57,512
That could help us,
don't you think?

1591
01:08:57,547 --> 01:08:59,411
-I can tell you
what kind of slippers there.

1592
01:08:59,445 --> 01:09:02,172
-Yes, that might just be
the solution.

1593
01:09:02,207 --> 01:09:04,726
We'll take them, but I don't
think she should find out.

1594
01:09:04,761 --> 01:09:08,661
We'd better do it all in secret.-Yeah. Secret.

1595
01:09:08,696 --> 01:09:12,527
-We'll get in disguise.
We'll be women.

1596
01:09:12,562 --> 01:09:15,841
-Yes. No I'm quite sure
it's embedded in the dirt.

1597
01:09:15,875 --> 01:09:17,256
-They're slippers.
-Of course,

1598
01:09:17,291 --> 01:09:19,396
it's a small quantity, doctor,but your suspicions are correct.

1599
01:09:19,431 --> 01:09:21,640
-They're pieces of marble.

1600
01:09:21,674 --> 01:09:23,193
-You're sure it's marble?

1601
01:09:23,228 --> 01:09:25,402
-Marble?
-Can you identify its source?

1602
01:09:25,437 --> 01:09:27,059
-Cat's eye.
-No, it isn't.

1603
01:09:27,093 --> 01:09:29,061
But it's a fine quality.
-Classy.

1604
01:09:29,095 --> 01:09:31,201
-It might be a Carrara marble.
I can say that.

1605
01:09:31,236 --> 01:09:32,685
-Maybe a puri.
-It's used in the construction

1606
01:09:32,720 --> 01:09:36,413
of mausoleums, as far as I know.

1607
01:09:36,448 --> 01:09:38,657
-♪ Ohh 
-Thank you.

1608
01:09:38,691 --> 01:09:41,038
-She went out late at night
and played marbles.

1609
01:09:41,073 --> 01:09:43,938
What could it mean?

1610
01:09:43,972 --> 01:09:47,528
♪♪

1611
01:09:47,562 --> 01:09:49,219
-Meanwhile,
back at the other set.

1612
01:09:49,254 --> 01:09:51,325
-Fortunately, it was still lit.

1613
01:09:51,359 --> 01:09:54,707
